IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `er2-common`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 19 to 21: the record of employment, and the hours and insurable
-- earnings it reports. Piece er2 (Sonnet 5.5), LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Every src:N below is a line of the Regulations' raw file
-- SOR-96-332.txt, an unofficial plain-text rendering made by a converter script; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- Conventions (eia-core NOTES.md): a time limit is a NUMBER of days and "not later than n days after d" ends on d PLUS n, that day
-- counting (fork F4 of the keel); a date is built with YMD; a fact decided outside this piece is a plain GIVEN, named for the fact and
-- marked "out of range: ... (piece X)". A DEADLINE is a DATE-valued rule and "in time" is a BOOLEAN rule over it; the duty itself is the
-- relation between the employer (who owes it) and the insured person or the Commission (to whom it is owed), named neutrally.

§ `Regulation 19 - Record of employment`

§§ `Regulation 19(1) - who is an employer in subsections (2) to (4)`

-- src:343 | 19 (1) In subsections (2) to (4), "employer" includes a bankrupt employer or the trustee of a bankrupt employer.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(1) (src:343)
GIVEN `is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has been an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the individual who is sponsor or co-ordinator of a project in paragraph 5(1)(e) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question concerns that individual's remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a bankrupt employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the trustee of a bankrupt employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 19(1) employer for the purposes of subsections (2) to (4)` IF
        `s 2(1) employer` `is an employer` `has been an employer` `is the individual who is sponsor or co-ordinator of a project in paragraph 5(1)(e) of the Act` `the question concerns that individual's remuneration`
    OR  `is a bankrupt employer`
    OR  `is the trustee of a bankrupt employer`

§§ `Regulation 19(2) - the duty to complete a record of employment`

-- src:344 | (2) Every employer shall complete a record of employment, on a form supplied by the Commission, in respect of a person employed by the employer in insurable employment who has an interruption of earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(2) (src:344)
GIVEN `an employer for the purposes of subsections (2) to (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed by the employer in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has an interruption of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- `an employer ...` is the result of reg 19(1) above.
-- out of range: section 5 (piece ei1 of the table in the brief; the core's `s 5 insurable employment` decides the second fact)
-- out of range: regulation 14 (piece er1), "interruption of earnings", s 2(1) of the Act
DECIDE `reg 19(2) a record of employment must be completed in respect of the person` IF
        `an employer for the purposes of subsections (2) to (4)`
    AND `the person is employed by the employer in insurable employment`
    AND `the person has an interruption of earnings`

§§ `Regulation 19(3) - copies of a record of employment completed on paper`

-- The time limit of paragraph (a), shared by paragraph (b): "not later than five days after the later of (i) and (ii)".
-- src:345 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), copies of the record of employment completed in paper form in accordance with subsection (2) shall be distributed by the employer in the following manner:
-- src:346 | (a) the employee's copy shall be delivered to the insured person not later than five days after the later of
-- src:347 | (i) the first day of the interruption of earnings, and
-- src:348 | (ii) the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(3)(a) (src:345-348)
GIVEN `the first day of the interruption of earnings` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 19(3)(a) the last day for delivering the employee's copy to the insured person` IS
    `the last day of` 5 `days after` (`er2 the later of two days` `the first day of the interruption of earnings` `the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings`)

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(3)(a) (src:346-348)
GIVEN `the first day of the interruption of earnings` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the employee's copy was delivered to the insured person` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 19(3)(a) the employee's copy was delivered in time` IF
    `the day on which the employee's copy was delivered to the insured person` AT MOST (`reg 19(3)(a) the last day for delivering the employee's copy to the insured person` `the first day of the interruption of earnings` `the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings`)

-- src:349 | (b) the Commission's copy shall be sent to the Commission within the time limit set out in paragraph (a); and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(3)(b) (src:349)
GIVEN `the first day of the interruption of earnings` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Commission's copy was sent to the Commission` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 19(3)(b) the Commission's copy was sent in time` IF
    `the day on which the Commission's copy was sent to the Commission` AT MOST (`reg 19(3)(a) the last day for delivering the employee's copy to the insured person` `the first day of the interruption of earnings` `the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings`)

-- src:350 | (c) the employer's copy shall be kept and retained as a part of the employer's records and books of account in accordance with subsection 87(3) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(3)(c) (src:350)
GIVEN `the employer's copy is kept and retained as a part of the employer's records and books of account in accordance with subsection 87(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: section 87(3) (piece ei3)
DECIDE `reg 19(3)(c) the employer's copy has been kept and retained` IF
    `the employer's copy is kept and retained as a part of the employer's records and books of account in accordance with subsection 87(3) of the Act`

§§ `Regulation 19(3.1) - a record of employment completed in electronic form`

-- "(a) it shall be sent to the Commission not later than the earlier of (i) five days after the end of the pay period during which the first
-- day of the employee's interruption of earnings fell, and (ii) if there are 13 or fewer pay periods per year under the employer's pay cycle,
-- 15 days after the first day of the interruption of earnings". Limb (ii) is a candidate only when the pay cycle has 13 or fewer periods.
-- src:351 | (3.1) The record of employment completed in electronic form in accordance with subsection (2) shall be distributed by the employer in the following manner:
-- src:352 | (a) it shall be sent to the Commission not later than the earlier of
-- src:353 | (i) five days after the end of the pay period during which the first day of the employee’s interruption of earnings fell, and
-- src:354 | (ii) if there are 13 or fewer pay periods per year under the employer’s pay cycle, 15 days after the first day of the interruption of earnings; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(3.1)(a) (src:351-354)
GIVEN `the last day of the pay period during which the first day of the interruption of earnings fell` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the interruption of earnings` IS A DATE
      `the number of pay periods per year under the employer's pay cycle` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
-- out of range: regulation 1(1) "pay period" (piece er1)
DECIDE `reg 19(3.1)(a) the last day for sending the electronic record of employment to the Commission` IS
    IF   `the number of pay periods per year under the employer's pay cycle` AT MOST 13
    THEN `er2 the earlier of two days` `limb (i)` `limb (ii)`
    ELSE `limb (i)`
    WHERE
        `limb (i)` MEANS `the last day of` 5 `days after` `the last day of the pay period during which the first day of the interruption of earnings fell`
        `limb (ii)` MEANS `the last day of` 15 `days after` `the first day of the interruption of earnings`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(3.1)(a) (src:352-354)
GIVEN `the last day of the pay period during which the first day of the interruption of earnings fell` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the interruption of earnings` IS A DATE
      `the number of pay periods per year under the employer's pay cycle` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the electronic record of employment was sent to the Commission` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 19(3.1)(a) the electronic record of employment was sent in time` IF
    `the day on which the electronic record of employment was sent to the Commission` AT MOST (`reg 19(3.1)(a) the last day for sending the electronic record of employment to the Commission` `the last day of the pay period during which the first day of the interruption of earnings fell` `the first day of the interruption of earnings` `the number of pay periods per year under the employer's pay cycle`)

-- src:355 | (b) it shall be kept and retained as part of the employer’s records and books of account in accordance with subsection 87(3) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(3.1)(b) (src:355)
GIVEN `the electronic record of employment is kept and retained as part of the employer's records and books of account in accordance with subsection 87(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: section 87(3) (piece ei3)
DECIDE `reg 19(3.1)(b) the electronic record of employment has been kept and retained` IF
    `the electronic record of employment is kept and retained as part of the employer's records and books of account in accordance with subsection 87(3) of the Act`

§§ `Regulation 19(4) - when the employee's copy cannot be delivered in time`

DECLARE `er2 Step the employer takes with an undelivered employee's copy` IS ONE OF
    `er2 mail the copy to the insured person`                                                                                              -- (a)
    `er2 retain the copy until the earliest of the Commission's request, the person's request and 52 weeks after completion`                -- (b)
    `er2 regulation 19(4) does not apply because delivery was not prevented for reasons beyond the employer's control`                      -- the text does not say what else

-- src:356 | (4) Where, for reasons beyond the employer's control, an employer is unable to deliver the employee's copy of the completed record of employment to the insured person within the time limit set out in paragraph (3)(a), the employer shall
-- src:357 | (a) where the employer knows the insured person's mailing address, mail the copy to that person; or
-- src:358 | (b) where the insured person's mailing address is not known to the employer, retain the copy until whichever of the following first occurs,
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(4) (src:356-358)
GIVEN `for reasons beyond the employer's control, the employer is unable to deliver the employee's copy to the insured person within the time limit set out in paragraph (3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer knows the insured person's mailing address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `er2 Step the employer takes with an undelivered employee's copy`
DECIDE `reg 19(4) what the employer must do with the employee's copy` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`for reasons beyond the employer's control, the employer is unable to deliver the employee's copy to the insured person within the time limit set out in paragraph (3)(a)`)
           THEN `er2 regulation 19(4) does not apply because delivery was not prevented for reasons beyond the employer's control`
           IF `the employer knows the insured person's mailing address`
           THEN `er2 mail the copy to the insured person`
           OTHERWISE `er2 retain the copy until the earliest of the Commission's request, the person's request and 52 weeks after completion`

-- (b)(i), (ii), (iii): the employer retains the copy until WHICHEVER OF THE THREE FIRST OCCURS. The last day of retention is therefore the
-- earliest of the day of the Commission's request (if any), the day of the person's request (if any) and the day 52 weeks after the
-- record of employment was completed (52 weeks = 364 days, s 2(1) "week").
-- src:359 | (i) the copy is requested by the Commission,
-- src:360 | (ii) the copy is requested by the person, or
-- src:361 | (iii) 52 weeks have elapsed since the record of employment was completed.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(4)(b) (src:358-361)
GIVEN `the day on which the record of employment was completed` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Commission requested the copy, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the insured person requested the copy, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 19(4)(b) the day on which the employer may stop retaining the copy` IS
    `er2 the earlier of two days` `the earlier of the two requests and 52 weeks` `the day of the person's request, or the last day of 52 weeks`
    WHERE
        `the day 52 weeks have elapsed` MEANS `the day on which the record of employment was completed` PLUS `weeks as days` 52
        `the day of the Commission's request, or the last day of 52 weeks` MEANS fromMaybe `the day 52 weeks have elapsed` `the day on which the Commission requested the copy, if it did`
        `the day of the person's request, or the last day of 52 weeks` MEANS fromMaybe `the day 52 weeks have elapsed` `the day on which the insured person requested the copy, if they did`
        `the earlier of the two requests and 52 weeks` MEANS `er2 the earlier of two days` `the day of the Commission's request, or the last day of 52 weeks` `the day 52 weeks have elapsed`

§§ `Regulation 19(5) - a statement of hours and insurable earnings`

-- "Where an employer has failed to deliver a record of employment to an insured person or to the Commission OR the employer is not
-- available OR is unable to provide information ... because the employer's records are destroyed or lost": four alternatives
-- (fork F1 in NOTES.md: "because ..." attached to the last alternative only).
-- src:362 | (5) Where an employer has failed to deliver a record of employment to an insured person or to the Commission or the employer is not available or is unable to provide information respecting the record of hours of insurable employment and the insurable earnings of that person because the employer's records are destroyed or lost, the person, on becoming a claimant, may provide, in respect of their hours of insurable employment and insurable earnings, a statement containing evidence of the hours and earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(5) (src:362)
GIVEN `the employer has failed to deliver a record of employment to the insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has failed to deliver a record of employment to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is not available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is unable to provide information respecting the record of hours of insurable employment and the insurable earnings of the person because the employer's records are destroyed or lost` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person applies for benefits under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has applied for benefits under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 19(5) the person may provide a statement of their hours of insurable employment and insurable earnings` IF
        (   `the employer has failed to deliver a record of employment to the insured person`
         OR `the employer has failed to deliver a record of employment to the Commission`
         OR `the employer is not available`
         OR `the employer is unable to provide information respecting the record of hours of insurable employment and the insurable earnings of the person because the employer's records are destroyed or lost`)
    AND `s 2(1) claimant` `the person applies for benefits under the Act` `the person has applied for benefits under the Act`

§§ `Regulation 19(6) - a bankrupt employer's records`

-- "has not provided a record of employment to an insured person or to the Commission": read as in (5), that is, to either of them
-- (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
-- src:363 | (6) Where a bankrupt employer or the trustee of a bankrupt employer has not provided a record of employment to an insured person or to the Commission, the Commission shall, in respect of that person, determine the number of hours of insurable employment and the amount of insurable earnings for benefit purposes on the basis of the payroll and personnel records of the bankrupt employer provided by the trustee.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 19(6) (src:363)
GIVEN `the employer is a bankrupt employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is the trustee of a bankrupt employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a record of employment has not been provided to the insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a record of employment has not been provided to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 19(6) the hours of insurable employment and insurable earnings are determined from the payroll and personnel records of the bankrupt employer` IF
        (`the employer is a bankrupt employer` OR `the employer is the trustee of a bankrupt employer`)
    AND (`a record of employment has not been provided to the insured person` OR `a record of employment has not been provided to the Commission`)

§ `Regulation 20 - Hours of insurable employment for a record of employment`

-- src:366 | 20 The number of hours of insurable employment reported in a record of employment with respect to an insured person shall be determined pursuant to Part I of the Act and any regulations made under that Part.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 20 (src:366)
GIVEN `the number of hours of insurable employment reported in the record of employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of hours of insurable employment determined pursuant to Part I of the Act and any regulations made under that Part` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: Part I of the Act and the regulations made under it (pieces ei1, ei2, er1, er3)
DECIDE `reg 20 the hours reported are the hours determined under Part I` IF
    `the number of hours of insurable employment reported in the record of employment` EQUALS `the number of hours of insurable employment determined pursuant to Part I of the Act and any regulations made under that Part`

§ `Regulation 21 - Insurable earnings for a record of employment`

-- src:369 | 21 The insurable earnings reported in a record of employment with respect to an insured person shall be determined pursuant to Parts III and IV of the Act and any regulations made under those Parts and allocated in accordance with section 23.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 21 (src:369)
GIVEN `the insurable earnings reported in the record of employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the insurable earnings determined pursuant to Parts III and IV of the Act and any regulations made under those Parts and allocated in accordance with section 23` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: Parts III and IV of the Act (pieces ei3 and the Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums Regulations, not deposited);
-- the allocation of section 23 is regulation 23 (module er2-allocation).
DECIDE `reg 21 the insurable earnings reported are the insurable earnings determined and allocated` IF
    `the insurable earnings reported in the record of employment` EQUALS `the insurable earnings determined pursuant to Parts III and IV of the Act and any regulations made under those Parts and allocated in accordance with section 23`
